  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $743M in FY2027 to date for federal contracts. The department made 1,787 awards with an average award size of $416K. Obligations fell 89.4% year over year compared with the prior fiscal period. Historically, Treasury obligated $9.3B in FY22, $10.3B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, $8.6B in FY25, and $7B in FY26. The FY2027 to date total is partial and covers the fiscal year to date. The largest single NAICS category in FY2027 to date is Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining at $281M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $149M. The top vendor in FY2027 to date is STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $281M, followed by FCN, INC. at $82.7M and ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $42.9M. This snapshot shows a much smaller current-year obligations total compared with prior full fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How large is Treasury's contracting program right now?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $743M in FY2027 to date. The department made 1,787 awards with an average award size of $416K. Obligations fell 89.4% year over year. Prior full-year obligations were $9.3B in FY22, $10.3B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, $8.6B in FY25, and $7B in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What is Treasury buying and who are the suppliers?",
        "body": "Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining is the largest NAICS category at $281M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $149M and Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $64.3M. Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services is $42.1M and Paper Mills is $34M. The top vendors are STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $281M, FCN, INC. at $82.7M, and ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $42.9M."
      }
    ]
